      "notes": [
        {
          "text": "The marine tariff was revised with effect from 15 June 2026 (BPTS revision 06); the fuel surcharge on pilotage is set by circular and was USD 0.22696 per GT from 1 October 2026. The version starts on 1 October 2026 because both apply from then.",
          "source": {
            "document": "fuel-surcharge-2026-10-01",
            "page": 1
          }
        },
        {
          "text": "Pilotage minimums change at 3,000 and 15,000 GT while the rate changes at 10,000 GT; bands are split so each carries its own minimum. 'Less than 10,000' is entered as up to 9,999.99 GT.",
          "source": {
            "document": "bpts-2026-06-15",
            "page": 30,
            "section": "IV.B"
          }
        },
        {
          "text": "The berth hire minimum of US$ 810 per day cannot be expressed per day in the format and is not applied; it only matters for ships under about 2,900 GT.",
          "source": {
            "document": "bpts-2026-06-15",
            "page": 31,
            "section": "IV.F"
          }
        },
        {
          "text": "The tariff is in US dollars for all ships; there are no separate coastal rates.",
          "source": {
            "document": "bpts-2026-06-15",
            "page": 30
          }
        },
        {
          "text": "The environment protection charge lists bulk, break-bulk, liquid, Ro-Ro and gas carriers, plus ships at the MICT (DP World) berths. It is not applied to container ships at other terminals.",
          "source": {
            "document": "bpts-2026-06-15",
            "page": 31,
            "section": "IV.E"
          }
        }
      ]
